Title:
lacuna-rs — Ghost-frame call-stack spoofing + runtime indirect syscalls for Windows x64 (Rust)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- `lacuna-rs` is a Rust crate port of the LACUNA Chain technique, providing primitives for ghost-frame call stack spoofing and runtime-resolved indirect syscalls on Windows x64.  
- It targets EDR detections that rely on userland hooks, syscall origin/SSN mismatches, and call-stack/ETW-Ti stackwalk correlation during injection and post-exploitation.  
- The crate implements PE/.pdata parsing and “ghost region” scanning, Hell’s Gate/Halo’s Gate-style SSN resolution, per-function `syscall;ret` targeting, and JIT emission of indirect syscall stubs.  
- Optional components add VEH + hardware-breakpoint parameter encryption (decrypting at the syscall boundary) and a multi-layer LACUNA ghost-frame chain with stack stomping (requires frame pointers in the consuming project).  
- It also includes a section-based APC injection implementation with a thread scoring algorithm to reduce instability from mass APC queueing.  
- Useful primarily for red teams, implant/tooling developers, and researchers evaluating call-stack-based detections and syscall telemetry.

Technical Focus:
- `.pdata` RUNTIME_FUNCTION gap (“ghost frame”) discovery and unwind-walk manipulation
- Runtime SSN resolution (Hell’s Gate / Halo’s Gate) and per-function `syscall;ret` selection
- JIT indirect syscall stub generation and gadget-based redirection (`jmp [rbx]`)
- VEH-based syscall parameter encryption using hardware breakpoints (DR0)
- LACUNA multi-layer spoofed call stack construction (wow64/kernelbase/ntdll/win32u layering)
- Section-based APC injection and thread selection/scoring via `NtQueryInformationThread`

Use Cases:
- Build Windows x64 Rust implants that avoid common userland-hook and syscall-origin heuristics
- Research/PoC for call-stack spoofing against ETW-Ti stackwalk and semantic stack analysis
- Runtime-safe syscall invocation across Windows builds without precomputed SSN tables
- Section-based APC injection with reduced crash risk via selective thread targeting
- Defensive validation: reproduce and test detections for ghost frames, indirect syscalls, and VEH/HWBP behaviors

Keywords:
Windows x64, Rust, LACUNA Chain, ghost frames, call stack spoofing, .pdata, RUNTIME_FUNCTION, unwind, indirect syscalls, syscall;ret, SSN resolution, Hell’s Gate, Halo’s Gate, ntdll, win32u, kernelbase, wow64, VEH, hardware breakpoints, DR0, ETW-Ti, APC injection, NtQueueApcThread, NtCreateSection, NtMapViewOfSection, NtWriteVirtualMemory, NtCreateThreadEx, litcrypt2, BYOUD-MF, BYOUD-RT, BYOUD-Gap